      "statusChangeNewStatus": "tracked",
      "value": "Thanks for your report.\n\nTechnically speaking, this is expected behavior. The Value attribute you set on an expressions entry (screenshot from your video attached) defines the value your animator parameter will be set to when the toggle or button is activated. When it's deactivated (turning the toggle off or shortly after pressing the button), the value is always set back to zero/false. So in this situation, the animator parameter is set to false both when the expression starts and when it stops.\n\nWe're looking into ways of improving how this is represented in the SDK. In the meantime, you should set the Value for your Boolean buttons and toggles back to true to avoid this issue. If you're trying to enable a feature/clothing/etc. on your avatar by default, consider inverting the meaning of your animator parameter so switching it to true causes the feature to disappear and vice versa.",
